# 📋 CI/CD Security Report Template

Security engineers should document pipeline weaknesses and remediation.

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| Finding ID | Unique finding identifier |
| Component | Pipeline, runner, dependency, artifact, or deployment |
| Vulnerability | Identified security weakness |
| Severity | Critical, High, Medium, or Low |
| Evidence | Technical evidence supporting the finding |
| Impact | Potential consequences |
| Remediation | Recommended fix |
| Owner | Responsible team or individual |
| Status | Open, In Progress, Fixed, or Verified |
| Validation | Evidence that the issue has been resolved |

### Example Finding

| Field | Example |
|---|---|
| Finding ID | CICD-001 |
| Component | GitHub Actions Workflow |
| Vulnerability | Excessive workflow permissions |
| Severity | High (illustrative) |
| Evidence | Workflow has write permissions that are not required for its tasks. |
| Impact | A compromised workflow may modify repository resources. |
| Remediation | Restrict permissions to the minimum required for each job. |
| Status | Fixed |
| Validation | Reviewed workflow permissions and confirmed unnecessary write access was removed. |

